{"duration_api_ms":136829,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"e25d97fb-5a14-4c91-a42c-2ac97527a1da","total_cost_usd":0.18921400000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15495,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":12723,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7451},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12723,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15495},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12723,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15495,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.18921400000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7451,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"All 12 feasible non-dominated designs sit at the same corner: bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg, D about 3.383-3.385 m. Only flight_path_angle varies along the front, from -1.5 deg (227k W/m2, 418 K) to -3.565 deg (274.6k W/m2, 391.2 K). Two constraints pin the corner. Heatshield mass fraction runs out at D about 3.385 m (margin falls roughly 0.6 per metre of D). max_g runs out at gamma about -3.57 deg. Eight of the geometry failures come from bluntness above 1.2 at cone 70, or from cone 69 at bluntness 1.2, so the aero surrogate's convex hull ends there. Round 2 wasted 18 evaluations by probing outside it.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-fb90f652dec5 through C-f71f4a44911d: on the front, flux rises and bondline temperature falls monotonically as gamma steepens at fixed D of about 3.383, b 1.2, cone 70.\",\"C-3583b7488cf2, C-2a109f1c4205 and C-053e6577c074 (all gamma -3.58/-3.6): max_g is slightly violated (12.002-12.016 against a 12 limit) while their mass margins are positive, so gamma about -3.565 is the g limit.\",\"C-6ffb6b7edb43 (3.384 m, margin 0.00074), C-1a745bbcb46d (3.385 m, margin 0.00014) and C-053e6577c074 (3.38 m, margin 0.0031): mass margin goes to zero near D of 3.3852.\",\"C-d883f15f56c5 (b 1.05, D 3.37, gamma -3.58): flux 284k against about 277.5k for b 1.2, with a worse bondline temperature and a lower mass margin. Higher bluntness therefore helps every metric.\",\"C-11ae4eb65bbb, C-660a8eef4199 and C-460ff98d4dde (b 1.24-1.25 at cone 70; b 1.2 at cone 69): 'cd_fore' extrapolation failure, so the hull boundary is at or near the (1.2, 70) vertex.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Peak flux scales roughly as sqrt(rho_peak/Rn). It falls with larger D (larger Rn and lower ballistic coefficient) and with higher bluntness. Bondline temperature follows the integrated heat load, which a steeper entry lowers. Peak g is set mainly by gamma (prior knowledge, consistent with the table). The corner is already at the surrogate's edge, so the front can only be refined. I do this by filling gamma gaps at D 3.385 and by probing interior bluntness and cone combinations. Those probes use convex combinations of evaluated points, so they should stay inside the hull and avoid no-geometry failures. I expect them to be dominated but informative about cone and bluntness sensitivity.\",\"uncertainty\":\"I cannot see the round-2 and round-3 points, so the effect of cone angle on flux, mass and g is unknown. The exact hull edge near (b 1.2, cone 70) is unknown, so proposal 13 could fail. The D 3.385 mass margin is only about 1e-4, so small sensitivities could flip feasibility. My flux and temperature predictions are interpolations along the gamma sweep, and I extrapolated them for the exploratory points.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill the gamma gap near the shallow end at D 3.385, the largest allowed diameter.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.6},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":229300,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":416.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the shallow end of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -1.7 and -1.9 at D 3.385.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.8},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":233400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -1.9 and -2.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.05},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":239000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":409.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -2.2 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":245900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":404.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -2.5 and -2.8.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.65},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":252700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":401.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -2.8 and -3.0.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":258700,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":398.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -3.0 and -3.2.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.1},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.9,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Fill gamma gap between -3.2 and -3.35.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.28},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":267800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.1,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Densify the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1a745bbcb46d\",\"rationale\":\"Steep end of the front at the largest D (3.385) and gamma just inside the g limit. The g margin at -3.55 was 0.0029 and at -3.565 was 0.0008.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.56},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Pushes the low-temperature end of the front at the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-af77f965ad8e\",\"rationale\":\"Shift D up by 0.0001 m to test the mass-fraction edge (predicted zero crossing near 3.3852) while gamma is -3.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3851,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":272900,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the mass-fraction limit more precisely.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d883f15f56c5\",\"rationale\":\"Interpolate bluntness between 1.05 and 1.2 at cone 70 (inside the hull by convexity) to see how flux and temperature scale with bluntness.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":277500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the bluntness gradient near the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d883f15f56c5\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.15 at cone 70, still on the hull edge between known-good points.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.45},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":275500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.4,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the mass margin allows a slightly larger D at intermediate bluntness.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-99e10ec941e7\",\"rationale\":\"Small step toward the hull corner (b 1.19, cone 69.95) to test the extrapolation boundary and cone sensitivity. It sits right on my estimated hull edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.19,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.95,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.8,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Reveals the local effect of cone angle and the hull edge shape at very low cost if it works.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d883f15f56c5\",\"rationale\":\"Lower cone angle at b 1.1 to measure cone sensitivity. This point should be well inside the hull.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.375,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":282000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cone-angle effect on flux, mass and g is unknown from the shown data.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d883f15f56c5\",\"rationale\":\"Moderate bluntness 1.0 and cone 69.2 as an interior probe for a possible different trade-off region.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.37,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.2,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":287000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether lower bluntness with lower cone gives any lower temperature at higher flux.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7e930f570744\",\"rationale\":\"Interior point between C-7e930f570744 and the corner (b 0.9, cone 66, D 3.3), with gamma moved inside the g limit, to explore a distinct region.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.3,\"bluntness_ratio\":0.9,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":66.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":300000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":394.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests the trend at lower bluntness and cone, away from the corner.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-7e930f570744\",\"rationale\":\"The same design with gamma moved from -4.54 to -3.5, to bring it inside the g limit and quantify what smaller D, b and cone cost.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":330000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":396.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Calibrates flux and temperature sensitivity to D, b and cone, and turns a nearly feasible point into a feasible reference.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d883f15f56c5\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.1 with cone 69.5 and D 3.38 at gamma just inside the g limit.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.38,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":280500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether the mass margin still allows D 3.38 at lower bluntness with a smaller cone angle, with gamma near the g limit.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-d883f15f56c5\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.0 at cone 70 with smaller D (3.36), which gives a healthy mass margin, to see how far flux degrades.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.36,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":290000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.5,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Extends the bluntness sweep at cone 70 to check the flux gradient.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-99e10ec941e7\",\"rationale\":\"Bluntness 1.15 and cone 69.3 at D 3.383 for a second cone-sensitivity point close to the corner, but away from the hull edge.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.3,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.2,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether a slightly lower cone angle reduces flux or mass fraction near the optimum.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":92551,"type":"result","duration_ms":136954,"uuid":"7409950d-ba5a-4069-a9f7-22ec2d5436d7","ttft_stream_ms":2049,"time_to_request_ms":127,"first_content_frame_ms":2049,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
